<section image-layout="blank" id="ORLDe9xU1a" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="HNahflIz6R"><h2>Hospitality onstage; choreography backstage</h2><p font-size="16pt"><b>Illustrative operating model</b> · 2 sessions/day · 8 places/session · 15-minute room turn</p><p font-size="16pt">Guests see a calm hour; backstage, one sequence governs inventory, room standards, qualified delivery, handoffs, and records.</p><table col-widths="[12,30,58]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 3pt 12pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p>Stage</p></td><td><p>Guest-facing lane</p></td><td><p>Backstage choreography and owner</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Offer</b></p></td><td><p>A clear, bookable ritual.</p></td><td><p><b>Reservations/front desk:</b> use one script and one shared inventory before arrival, at check-in, or in stay.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Prepare</b></p></td><td><p>A room that feels ready.</p></td><td><p><b>Hotel host:</b> checks accessible route, water, linens, seating, temperature, and approved materials.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Deliver</b></p></td><td><p>A warm welcome and guided hour.</p></td><td><p><b>Practitioner:</b> owns practice and safety boundaries. <b>Host:</b> owns welcome and handoff.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Reset</b></p></td><td><p>A consistent room at every session.</p></td><td><p><b>Hotel host:</b> restores the documented room standard before inventory reopens.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Learn</b></p></td><td><p>A brief, respectful follow-up.</p></td><td><p><b>Pilot owner:</b> logs attendance, anonymous feedback, staff handling time, direct costs—no unnecessary health data.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item></grid></section>